{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"violinY"},{"type":"text","value":" draws vertical mirrored profiles around categorical x centers.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"violinX"},{"type":"text","value":" transposes the contract around categorical y centers."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { violinY } from '@tanstack/charts/violin'\n\nviolinY(profileRows, {\n  x: 'category',\n  y: 'position',\n  width: 'width',\n  span: 0.8,\n  color: 'category',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both marks are also exported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/universal"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"prepared-profiles-and-summaries","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prepared profiles and summaries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The mark mirrors prepared normalized widths. It does not choose bins, estimate\na density, normalize values, or calculate summaries."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const bins = binY(rows, {\n  value: 'body_mass_g',\n  by: 'species',\n  thresholds: massBoundaries,\n  outputs: { count: { reduce: 'count' } },\n})\nconst profiles = normalize(bins, {\n  value: 'count',\n  by: 'species',\n  basis: 'max',\n  as: 'width',\n})\nconst summaries = groupBy(rows, {\n  by: 'species',\n  outputs: {\n    median: { value: 'body_mass_g', reduce: median },\n  },\n})\n\ndefineChart({\n  marks: [\n    violinY(profiles, {\n      x: 'species',\n      y: 'y',\n      width: 'width',\n      span: 0.76,\n      color: 'species',\n      curve: d3AreaXCurve(curveBasis),\n    }),\n    tickY(summaries, {\n      x: 'species',\n      y: 'median',\n      span: 0.36,\n    }),\n    dot(summaries, { x: 'species', y: 'median' }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: {\n      scale: scalePoint<string>().domain(species).padding(0.5),\n    },\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear },\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This example is a normalized histogram profile. A kernel density estimate can\nfeed the same mark, but its kernel and bandwidth remain data-preparation policy."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":" must be finite and within "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[0, 1]"},{"type":"text","value":". Nullish and nonfinite profile\npositions or widths create gaps. Sort samples into the intended profile order\nbefore passing them to the mark."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"signatures","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Signatures"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function violinY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: ViolinYOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum>\n\nfunction violinX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: ViolinXOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum>","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The profile position is numeric or temporal. The category is a numeric or\nstring "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartKey"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The public type surface includes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ViolinPosition"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ViolinYCurve"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ViolinXCurve"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ViolinYOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ViolinXOptions"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required by Y"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Categorical center for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"violinY"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, number | Date?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required by Y"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vertical profile position for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"violinY"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, number | Date?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required by X"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Horizontal profile position for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"violinX"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required by X"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Categorical center for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"violinX"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, number?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Normalized mirrored envelope width"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"span"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0.8"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Full peak width in category-step units"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Layer-derived"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable mark ID"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inferred"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable profile-sample identity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"color"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Category"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Value sent to the chart color scale"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fill"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stroke"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VisualChannel<TDatum, string>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resolved color"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Envelope paint; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stroke: null"},{"type":"text","value":" omits the outline"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fillOpacity"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeOpacity"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeWidth"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renderer default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Envelope presentation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeDasharray"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Outline dash pattern"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"curve"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ViolinYCurve"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ViolinXCurve"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Straight"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Orientation-specific renderer-neutral area path generator"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"states"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"readonly ChartMarkState[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Focus-driven area styles"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkMotionOptions<TDatum>['motion']"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keyed envelope motion policy"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"span"},{"type":"text","value":" must be positive and finite. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"span: 1"},{"type":"text","value":" makes a peak one complete\ncategory step wide. Values above "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"},{"type":"text","value":" can overlap adjacent categories."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"d3AreaXCurve(curveBasis)"},{"type":"text","value":" for a curved "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"violinY"},{"type":"text","value":". Use\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"d3Curve(curveBasis)"},{"type":"text","value":" for a curved "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"violinX"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"category-scale-identity-and-interaction","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Category scale, identity, and interaction"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The categorical axis must resolve to a point or band scale. Width uses the\nsmallest step in the complete configured domain, including categories without\nprofile rows. A single-category profile uses a bounded plot-relative fallback."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each valid sample contributes one interaction point at its semantic category\ncenter even though the envelope has two painted boundaries. The point retains\nthe exact source datum and index. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"violinY"},{"type":"text","value":" reports the category as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"xValue"},{"type":"text","value":"\nand profile position as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"yValue"},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"violinX"},{"type":"text","value":" transposes them. Use an explicit\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"},{"type":"text","value":" when positions repeat within a category."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"prepared-profiles-and-summaries","text":"Prepared profiles and summaries","level":2},{"id":"signatures","text":"Signatures","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"category-scale-identity-and-interaction","text":"Category scale, identity, and interaction","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n`violinY` draws vertical mirrored profiles around categorical x centers.\n`violinX` transposes the contract around categorical y centers.\n\n```ts\nimport { violinY } from '@tanstack/charts/violin'\n\nviolinY(profileRows, {\n  x: 'category',\n  y: 'position',\n  width: 'width',\n  span: 0.8,\n  color: 'category',\n})\n```\n\nBoth marks are also exported from `@tanstack/charts` and\n`@tanstack/charts/universal`.\n\n## Prepared profiles and summaries\n\nThe mark mirrors prepared normalized widths. It does not choose bins, estimate\na density, normalize values, or calculate summaries.\n\n```ts\nconst bins = binY(rows, {\n  value: 'body_mass_g',\n  by: 'species',\n  thresholds: massBoundaries,\n  outputs: { count: { reduce: 'count' } },\n})\nconst profiles = normalize(bins, {\n  value: 'count',\n  by: 'species',\n  basis: 'max',\n  as: 'width',\n})\nconst summaries = groupBy(rows, {\n  by: 'species',\n  outputs: {\n    median: { value: 'body_mass_g', reduce: median },\n  },\n})\n\ndefineChart({\n  marks: [\n    violinY(profiles, {\n      x: 'species',\n      y: 'y',\n      width: 'width',\n      span: 0.76,\n      color: 'species',\n      curve: d3AreaXCurve(curveBasis),\n    }),\n    tickY(summaries, {\n      x: 'species',\n      y: 'median',\n      span: 0.36,\n    }),\n    dot(summaries, { x: 'species', y: 'median' }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: {\n      scale: scalePoint<string>().domain(species).padding(0.5),\n    },\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThis example is a normalized histogram profile. A kernel density estimate can\nfeed the same mark, but its kernel and bandwidth remain data-preparation policy.\n\n`width` must be finite and within `[0, 1]`. Nullish and nonfinite profile\npositions or widths create gaps. Sort samples into the intended profile order\nbefore passing them to the mark.\n\n## Signatures\n\n```ts\nfunction violinY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: ViolinYOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum>\n\nfunction violinX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: ViolinXOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum>\n```\n\nThe profile position is numeric or temporal. The category is a numeric or\nstring `ChartKey`.\n\nThe public type surface includes `ViolinPosition`, `ViolinYCurve`,\n`ViolinXCurve`, `ViolinYOptions`, and `ViolinXOptions`.\n\n## Options\n\n| Option                                            | Type                                       | Default          | Meaning                                                   |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `x`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`               | Required by Y    | Categorical center for `violinY`                          |\n| `y`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, number \\| Date?>`         | Required by Y    | Vertical profile position for `violinY`                   |\n| `x`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, number \\| Date?>`         | Required by X    | Horizontal profile position for `violinX`                 |\n| `y`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`               | Required by X    | Categorical center for `violinX`                          |\n| `width`                                           | `Channel<TDatum, number?>`                 | Required         | Normalized mirrored envelope width                        |\n| `span`                                            | `number`                                   | `0.8`            | Full peak width in category-step units                    |\n| `id`                                              | `string`                                   | Layer-derived    | Stable mark ID                                            |\n| `key`                                             | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>`                | Inferred         | Stable profile-sample identity                            |\n| `color`                                           | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`               | Category         | Value sent to the chart color scale                       |\n| `fill`, `stroke`                                  | `VisualChannel<TDatum, string>`            | Resolved color   | Envelope paint; `stroke: null` omits the outline          |\n| `fillOpacity`, `strokeOpacity`, and `strokeWidth` | `number`                                   | Renderer default | Envelope presentation                                     |\n| `strokeDasharray`                                 | `string`                                   | None             | Outline dash pattern                                      |\n| `curve`                                           | `ViolinYCurve` or `ViolinXCurve`           | Straight         | Orientation-specific renderer-neutral area path generator |\n| `states`                                          | `readonly ChartMarkState[]`                | None             | Focus-driven area styles                                  |\n| `motion`                                          | `ChartMarkMotionOptions<TDatum>['motion']` | None             | Keyed envelope motion policy                              |\n\n`span` must be positive and finite. `span: 1` makes a peak one complete\ncategory step wide. Values above `1` can overlap adjacent categories.\n\nUse `d3AreaXCurve(curveBasis)` for a curved `violinY`. Use\n`d3Curve(curveBasis)` for a curved `violinX`.\n\n## Category scale, identity, and interaction\n\nThe categorical axis must resolve to a point or band scale. Width uses the\nsmallest step in the complete configured domain, including categories without\nprofile rows. A single-category profile uses a bounded plot-relative fallback.\n\nEach valid sample contributes one interaction point at its semantic category\ncenter even though the envelope has two painted boundaries. The point retains\nthe exact source datum and index. `violinY` reports the category as `xValue`\nand profile position as `yValue`; `violinX` transposes them. Use an explicit\n`key` when positions repeat within a category.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Violin Marks\ndescription: Reference for semantic violinY and violinX mirrored profile geometry, category-relative spans, curves, identity, and interaction.\n---\n\n`violinY` draws vertical mirrored profiles around categorical x centers.\n`violinX` transposes the contract around categorical y centers.\n\n```ts\nimport { violinY } from '@tanstack/charts/violin'\n\nviolinY(profileRows, {\n  x: 'category',\n  y: 'position',\n  width: 'width',\n  span: 0.8,\n  color: 'category',\n})\n```\n\nBoth marks are also exported from `@tanstack/charts` and\n`@tanstack/charts/universal`.\n\n## Prepared profiles and summaries\n\nThe mark mirrors prepared normalized widths. It does not choose bins, estimate\na density, normalize values, or calculate summaries.\n\n```ts\nconst bins = binY(rows, {\n  value: 'body_mass_g',\n  by: 'species',\n  thresholds: massBoundaries,\n  outputs: { count: { reduce: 'count' } },\n})\nconst profiles = normalize(bins, {\n  value: 'count',\n  by: 'species',\n  basis: 'max',\n  as: 'width',\n})\nconst summaries = groupBy(rows, {\n  by: 'species',\n  outputs: {\n    median: { value: 'body_mass_g', reduce: median },\n  },\n})\n\ndefineChart({\n  marks: [\n    violinY(profiles, {\n      x: 'species',\n      y: 'y',\n      width: 'width',\n      span: 0.76,\n      color: 'species',\n      curve: d3AreaXCurve(curveBasis),\n    }),\n    tickY(summaries, {\n      x: 'species',\n      y: 'median',\n      span: 0.36,\n    }),\n    dot(summaries, { x: 'species', y: 'median' }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: {\n      scale: scalePoint<string>().domain(species).padding(0.5),\n    },\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThis example is a normalized histogram profile. A kernel density estimate can\nfeed the same mark, but its kernel and bandwidth remain data-preparation policy.\n\n`width` must be finite and within `[0, 1]`. Nullish and nonfinite profile\npositions or widths create gaps. Sort samples into the intended profile order\nbefore passing them to the mark.\n\n## Signatures\n\n```ts\nfunction violinY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: ViolinYOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum>\n\nfunction violinX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: ViolinXOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum>\n```\n\nThe profile position is numeric or temporal. The category is a numeric or\nstring `ChartKey`.\n\nThe public type surface includes `ViolinPosition`, `ViolinYCurve`,\n`ViolinXCurve`, `ViolinYOptions`, and `ViolinXOptions`.\n\n## Options\n\n| Option                                            | Type                                       | Default          | Meaning                                                   |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `x`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`               | Required by Y    | Categorical center for `violinY`                          |\n| `y`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, number \\| Date?>`         | Required by Y    | Vertical profile position for `violinY`                   |\n| `x`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, number \\| Date?>`         | Required by X    | Horizontal profile position for `violinX`                 |\n| `y`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`               | Required by X    | Categorical center for `violinX`                          |\n| `width`                                           | `Channel<TDatum, number?>`                 | Required         | Normalized mirrored envelope width                        |\n| `span`                                            | `number`                                   | `0.8`            | Full peak width in category-step units                    |\n| `id`                                              | `string`                                   | Layer-derived    | Stable mark ID                                            |\n| `key`                                             | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>`                | Inferred         | Stable profile-sample identity                            |\n| `color`                                           | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`               | Category         | Value sent to the chart color scale                       |\n| `fill`, `stroke`                                  | `VisualChannel<TDatum, string>`            | Resolved color   | Envelope paint; `stroke: null` omits the outline          |\n| `fillOpacity`, `strokeOpacity`, and `strokeWidth` | `number`                                   | Renderer default | Envelope presentation                                     |\n| `strokeDasharray`                                 | `string`                                   | None             | Outline dash pattern                                      |\n| `curve`                                           | `ViolinYCurve` or `ViolinXCurve`           | Straight         | Orientation-specific renderer-neutral area path generator |\n| `states`                                          | `readonly ChartMarkState[]`                | None             | Focus-driven area styles                                  |\n| `motion`                                          | `ChartMarkMotionOptions<TDatum>['motion']` | None             | Keyed envelope motion policy                              |\n\n`span` must be positive and finite. `span: 1` makes a peak one complete\ncategory step wide. Values above `1` can overlap adjacent categories.\n\nUse `d3AreaXCurve(curveBasis)` for a curved `violinY`. Use\n`d3Curve(curveBasis)` for a curved `violinX`.\n\n## Category scale, identity, and interaction\n\nThe categorical axis must resolve to a point or band scale. Width uses the\nsmallest step in the complete configured domain, including categories without\nprofile rows. A single-category profile uses a bounded plot-relative fallback.\n\nEach valid sample contributes one interaction point at its semantic category\ncenter even though the envelope has two painted boundaries. The point retains\nthe exact source datum and index. `violinY` reports the category as `xValue`\nand profile position as `yValue`; `violinX` transposes them. Use an explicit\n`key` when positions repeat within a category.\n"}
